{%- comment -%}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RELEASE CALENDAR ROW (custom vcollect)

One row of the release calendar. Extracted into a snippet because sections/release-calendar.liquid renders its rows from
two separate ordered lists (dated first, then undated), and a duplicated row template is a duplicated bug.

  block - the section block of type "release"

The set name is a <th scope="row">: it is what identifies the row, and a machine reading the table needs to know that.
The release date carries data-sort-value in ISO form so the visible French date can still sort chronologically, and a
<time datetime> so the date is machine-readable in the served HTML rather than only in the JSON-LD.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

<tr {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <th scope="row">{{ block.settings.set_name | escape }}</th>
  <td>{{ block.settings.language | escape }}</td>
  <td data-sort-value="{{ block.settings.release_date }}">
    {%- if block.settings.release_date != blank -%}
      <time datetime="{{ block.settings.release_date }}">{{ block.settings.release_date | date: '%d/%m/%Y' }}</time>
    {%- else -%}
      {{- 'calendar.date_unannounced' | t -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  </td>
  <td>
    {%- if block.settings.products != blank -%}
      <ul class="citable-table__links">
        {%- for product in block.settings.products -%}
          <li><a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title | escape }}</a></li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    {%- endif -%}
  </td>
</tr>
